#
# Elecrow DIS08070H (CrowPanel ESP32 HMI 7.0") flash modules - the console, the external RAM
#
# The clock (dmclk) is the one of the mcu (configs/mcu/esp32s3/esp32s3fn16r8/flash.dmd).
#
# The console: UART0 on the pads of the ROM's console (GPIO43 TX, GPIO44 RX) that the USB-UART bridge of the board is wired to, 921600 8N1
# (board/elecrow-dis08070h/uart0.ini of dmuart); dmtty attaches a tty to it, so the shell runs there. /dev/ttyUSB0 on the host.
dmuart driver=board/elecrow-dis08070h/uart0.ini

#
# The external RAM: the 8 MB octal PSRAM of the module (WROOM-1-N4R8) behind the memory SPI (dmqspi), mapped into the address space and put
# at the end of the default heaps (it needs the clock of dmclk: driver_order). The bus runs at 40 MHz DDR (board/elecrow-dis08070h.ini of dmpsram):
# the display scans its frame buffer out of the PSRAM, 12 MHz * 2 bytes per pixel is more than the octal bus does at 20 MHz.
dmqspi
dmpsram driver=board/elecrow-dis08070h.ini

#
# /ext is the last 1.9 MB of the 4 MB flash of the module (0x220000, board.cmake). dmflash exports it as the block node
# /dev/dmflashx/ext (the firmware does the erasing and programming from the internal RAM with the caches off: dmod-boot,
# src/arch/xtensa/lx7/flash.c), dmlittlefs keeps a littlefs on it, which the "ext" service (services/ext.ini) mounts at /ext.
# A new flash has no file system: create it once with `mklittlefs /dev/dmflashx/ext` (ALL DATA IN IT IS LOST), or with
# `cmake --build <dir> --target format-ext`.
dmflash driver=board/elecrow-dis08070h/flash.ini
dmlittlefs
mklittlefs

#
# The microSD card, in its SPI mode (dmsdio, bus=spi: board/elecrow-dis08070h/sdspi.ini of dmsdio): the slot is wired to the SPI lines
# (SCK GPIO12, MOSI GPIO11, MISO GPIO13, CS GPIO10), the bus is the dmspi of the ini (GP-SPI2, all its own, the transfers go by dmdma), the chip
# select a dmgpio output. dmsdio reports the card as a block device (/dev/dmsdio0/0, a node that appears when a card is found: there is no detect
# line, dmdevmon looks for it every second).
# automount (dmblock) mounts every FAT/exFAT volume dmdevfs reports as a block device at /mnt/<label> (or /mnt/<node name>) and unmounts it when the
# card is gone; dmfatfs is the file system. A new card has none: create it once with `mkfatfs -t fat32 /dev/dmsdio0/0` (ALL DATA ON THE CARD IS LOST);
# the volume is then /mnt/dmsdio0_0p1.
dmdma driver=mcu/esp32s3.ini
dmgpio
dmspi
dmsdio driver=board/elecrow-dis08070h/sdspi.ini
dmfatfs
mkfatfs
automount service=automount@.ini
automount rules=automount.rules

#
# The display: 7.0" 800x480 RGB panel on the LCD_CAM peripheral (RGB565, 12 MHz pixel clock, ~25 Hz) with the frame buffer in the PSRAM, fed by
# the GDMA (dmdma, above) and restarted at every vertical sync (board/elecrow-dis08070h/lcd.ini of dmlcdtft). The ini also switches the
# backlight on (IO2, dmgpio). The splash logo (board.cmake, DMBOOT_SPLASH_LOGO) is shown as soon as the driver is up. The touch panel
# (GT911 behind the PCA9557 expander on I2C) has no driver yet.
dmlcdtft driver=board/elecrow-dis08070h/lcd.ini
